help.coordinates=Shows the position of the cell under the cursor as a **cell number, in pixels, and in UV**.
help.uvFormat=Chooses **which way V runs**.\n[fig:uv]\n**DirectX**: the origin is at the top left, and V grows downward.\n**OpenGL**: the origin is at the bottom left, and V grows upward. Unity uses this direction.
help.animationChips=Switches sheet images in order to make an **animated tile**.\n[fig:frames]\nFrames line up **left to right** on the sheet and play in that order. **Right-click any frame** to select the animation for placement.\nTo choose the frames, **Shift+left-click** a range on the sheet and use **Assign** from the right-click menu.\nChange the speed with each row's **FPS** (frames shown per second).
help.normalize=Corrects the width and height of an image to the nearest of **0.25×, 0.5×, or 1× to 8×** the base cell.\n**The original images are not changed.** The corrected size is saved in the project.
help.blackTransparency=Makes **black areas transparent**. Pixels become partly transparent according to their brightness.\nSuits light or fire effects drawn on black.
help.exportNumbers=**Draws a frame and the cell number** on each cell of the exported image.\nUse it to check UVs and numbers. **Turn it off** when exporting for use.
help.align4=Makes the exported width and height **multiples of 4**, adding **transparent space** on the right and bottom (tiles do not move).\nCompressed formats such as DirectX block compression work in 4×4 pixel blocks, so the width and height must be multiples of 4. The sheet preview shows it too.
help.hints=Shows the **hints that appear on hover**. Turn it off to see the coordinate card and similar displays more clearly.\n**The ? help still appears when this is off.**
tooltip.mapSheet=> Right-click|Choose the tile to place\n> Right-click and hold|Set as base cell or delete\n> Left-click and hold|Lift and reorder (on the selection, the whole selection)\n> Shift+left-drag|Select the tiles inside the dragged box (it can start on empty space)\n> Shift+left-click|Select the box between this tile and the last one\n> Shift+left-drag on the selection|Move it together, keeping its shape\n> Delete or Backspace|Delete the selected range (asks first)\nRight-click the selected range to **assign** it to an animation.
tooltip.mapCanvas=> Right-click|Place a tile\n> Left-drag|Move the view\n> Shift+left-drag|Select a range\n> Right-click in the range|Place on the whole range or use the tool\n> Delete or Backspace|Delete the tiles in the range (asks first)\nRight-click the tile at the top right to switch to the **tools** (erase, move, rotate, flip).
tooltip.animationIcon=**Select this animation** for placement.
tooltip.removeNormalization=Clears the **correction or ignore setting** and returns to the original size (the original image is kept).
